{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BringsSurface.HyperellipticQuintic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BringsSurface.HyperellipticQuintic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Circle"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.fifthRoot_is_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.fifthRoot_is_root","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/hyperelliptic-quintic.lean#L70-L80","doc":"Each fifth-root of unity is a root of x⁵ = 1.\n`(exp(2πi·k/5))^5 = exp(5 · 2πi·k/5) = exp(2πi·k) = (exp(2πi))^k = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.zeta5_pow_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.zeta5_pow_five","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/hyperelliptic-quintic.lean#L57-L68","doc":"ζ₅ raised to the fifth power is 1, since\nexp(2π i / 5)^5 = exp(2π i) = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.fifthRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.fifthRoot","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/hyperelliptic-quintic.lean#L48-L55","doc":"The `k`-th fifth-root of unity as a complex number.\n\nThe coercion `(k.val : ℂ)` is essential: using `k.val / 5`\nwould be integer division on `ℕ`, which evaluates to `0` for\nevery `k ∈ Fin 5` and would make every `fifthRoot k = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.quinticDefining","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.quinticDefining","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/hyperelliptic-quintic.lean#L43-L46","doc":"The defining polynomial P(x) = x⁵ - 1 of the double cover. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HyperellipticQuintic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HyperellipticQuintic","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/hyperelliptic-quintic.lean#L29-L41","doc":"**The hyperelliptic quintic 𝒳₅**: the affine plane curve\ny² = x⁵ - 1 in ℂ².  Represented as a predicate on pairs\n(x, y) ∈ ℂ × ℂ; the smooth projective completion adds one\npoint at infinity.\n\nIts six branch points under x ↦ x are the five fifth-roots of\nunity ζ₅^k (k = 0, ..., 4) together with ∞.  By Riemann-Hurwitz\nthe genus is (6 - 2)/2 = 2.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:hyperelliptic-quintic}`\nRef: [bolza1887] https://doi.org/10.2307/2369402 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.zeta5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.zeta5","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/hyperelliptic-quintic.lean#L24-L27","doc":"**Primitive fifth root of unity** ζ₅ = exp(2π i / 5). ","signatureChunk":0}]}